        </div>
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
          20&prime; Front + 30&prime; Rear + 15&prime; Side Setbacks Carve Up the Lot
        </h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Pre-zoning triple-deckers sit 10 feet from the street and 4 feet from side lot lines. Today&rsquo;s rules
          demand a <strong>20-foot front yard</strong>, <strong>30-foot rear yard</strong>, <strong
            >10 feet of separation from neighboring buildings</strong
          >, and <strong>15 feet of combined side yards</strong>&mdash;shrinking a 40&prime; wide lot down to a
          25&prime; wide buildable strip.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50/70 dark:bg-indigo-950/25 border border-indigo-200 dark:border-indigo-900/60"
      >
        <div class="text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-700 dark:text-indigo-400 mb-1">
